SLASH local modification to the pinned QDMA submodule (libqdma).

libqdma: queues serviced by their user (uld_service)

The SLASH NIC netdev (slash_nic.c) services its ST C2H queues from a NAPI
poll: qdma_queue_service() with a budget, then qdma_queue_update_pointers().
In POLL_MODE, qdma_queue_start() puts every queue on a libqdma completion
thread; for these queues the thread would be a second consumer of the
completion ring.

- qdma_queue_conf.uld_service: qdma_queue_start() does not add the queue to
  a completion thread. Unlike ext_producer, everything else is as usual (the
  host initialises the PIDX and posts the descriptors).
  qdma_thread_remove_work() already copes with a queue that was never added.

Applies on top of 0004-libqdma-ext-producer.patch.
Generated against qdma_drv @ 03ac7f3 (pinned submodule commit).
diff -ru a/libqdma_export.c b/libqdma_export.c
--- a/libqdma_export.c
+++ b/libqdma_export.c
@@ -1845,8 +1845,10 @@
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev_intr_info_list->vec_q_list, flags);
 	}
 
-	/* external producer: nobody in the host services this queue */
-	if (!descq->conf.ext_producer)
+	/* external producer: nobody in the host services this queue;
+	 * uld_service: its user services it (e.g. a NAPI poll)
+	 */
+	if (!descq->conf.ext_producer && !descq->conf.uld_service)
 		qdma_thread_add_work(descq);
 
 	snprintf(buf, buflen, "queue %s, idx %u started\n",
diff -ru a/libqdma_export.h b/libqdma_export.h
--- a/libqdma_export.h
+++ b/libqdma_export.h
@@ -667,6 +667,12 @@
 	 *   with init_pidx_dis for ST C2H.
 	 */
 	u8 ext_producer:1;
+	/**  Serviced by its user: the host owns the queue as usual (PIDX
+	 *   initialised, descriptors posted), but only the user calls
+	 *   qdma_queue_service() / qdma_queue_update_pointers() on it, e.g.
+	 *   from a NAPI poll. libqdma keeps it off the completion threads.
+	 */
+	u8 uld_service:1;
 
 	/**  MM Channel */
 	u8 mm_channel:1;
